## 1. Conditional / IF-type

*"What if X?" "Do Y, otherwise Z."*

| Phrase | Meaning | Dev example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Otherwise** | if not → nếu không | *"Refresh the token, **otherwise** the request will fail with 401."* |
| **Or else** | otherwise (casual) | *"We need to merge today, **or else** we'll block the release."* |
| **In case** | phòng khi | *"I added a retry **in case** the network drops."* |
| **As long as** | miễn là | *"It works **as long as** the user has a valid session."* |
| **Even if** | kể cả nếu | *"**Even if** the cache fails, the app still loads."* |

**Mini-drill:** rewrite each in 1 sentence about your current repo.

---

## 2. Contrast — BUT / HOWEVER family

*"I agree, but…" "It works, however…"*

| Phrase | Register | Dev example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **However** | formal (better than `but` in PR comments) | *"The fix works. **However,** it adds 200ms to startup."* |
| **Though / Although** | neutral | *"**Although** the API is stable, the UI still glitches."* |
| **Even though** | emphatic | *"**Even though** I added memoization, the list still re-renders."* |
| **Nonetheless / Nevertheless** | strong formal | *"The approach is risky. **Nevertheless,** it's the fastest option."* |
| **Still** | very spoken, natural | *"I was tired. **Still,** I shipped the PR."* |
| **On the other hand** | balancing trade-offs | *"REST is simpler. **On the other hand,** GraphQL gives us typed contracts."* |

**Senior habit:** in code review comments, use **`However,`** or **`That said,`** — sounds balanced, not aggressive. Avoid bare `but` at the start of a review.

---

## 3. Addition — ADD MORE

*"Also, …" "Besides, …"*

| Phrase | Position | Dev example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Also** | middle / start | *"We should fix the bug. **Also,** the test is flaky."* |
| **As well** | end of sentence | *"I'll update the docs **as well**."* |
| **Besides** | casual, add a reason | *"It's faster. **Besides,** it's easier to test."* |
| **In addition** | formal | *"**In addition** to the retry, we added circuit breaker logic."* |
| **Plus** | very US, casual | *"It's cheap. **Plus,** it works great."* |

**Note:** in spoken English, `also` and `plus` dominate. `In addition` is rare in standup; save it for docs/ADRs.

---

## 4. Cause / Result

*"…because …" "…, so …"*

| Phrase | Use when | Dev example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Because** | direct cause | *"I rolled back **because** the error rate spiked."* |
| **Since** | softer "because" | *"**Since** the API is down, I'll mock the response."* |
| **So** | casual result (very common) | *"CI is failing, **so** I'll debug first."* |
| **That's why** | emphatic result | *"The token wasn't persisted. **That's why** the login kept failing."* |
| **Therefore** | formal (ADRs, docs) | *"The cost exceeds the benefit. **Therefore,** we'll defer this."* |
| **As a result** | formal consequence | *"Queries were uncached. **As a result,** we hit the API 10× more."* |

**Pattern to memorize first: `…, so …`** — this single linker covers ~40% of your daily standup needs.

---

## 5. Examples / Explanation

*"For example…" "In other words…"*

| Phrase | Register | Dev example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **For example / For instance** | neutral | *"We have performance issues — **for example,** the feed re-renders on every scroll."* |
| **Such as** | listing items | *"Errors **such as** 401 and 403 trigger a logout."* |
| **Like** | very US, casual | *"Frameworks **like** RN and Flutter have similar trade-offs."* |
| **In other words** | clarify / rephrase | *"He's not available — **in other words,** we have to ship without him."* |

**When explaining a bug, always have one example ready.** Senior devs don't speak abstractly — they ground every claim in a concrete case.

---

## 6. Time / Sequence

*"First, then, after that, finally."*

| Phrase | Position in flow | Dev example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **First** | opener | *"**First,** I reproduced the bug locally."* |
| **Then / After that** | next step | *"**Then,** I checked the Sentry logs."* |
| **Before** | prerequisite | *"**Before** I deployed, I ran the tests."* |
| **While** | simultaneous | *"I debugged the UI **while** the backend team fixed the API."* |
| **Meanwhile** | parallel action | *"**Meanwhile,** the staging env was still broken."* |
| **Eventually** | final outcome | *"**Eventually,** we traced it to a caching bug."* |

**Incident timeline template (Day 25 preview):**
> *"**First,** alerts fired at 10:03. **Then,** I checked Sentry — CPU spike. **Meanwhile,** the on-call engineer rolled back. **Eventually,** we identified a memory leak in the new feature."*

