## 7. Emphasis — very US

*"Actually, honestly, basically…"*

| Phrase | Meaning | Dev example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Actually** | correct a misconception | *"**Actually,** the bug is in the selector, not the reducer."* |
| **Basically** | simplify | *"**Basically,** the hook runs twice on mount."* |
| **Literally** | emphasize (don't overuse!) | *"The app **literally** crashes on the login screen."* |
| **Seriously** | strong commitment | *"**Seriously,** this is the third time this week."* |
| **Honestly** | sincerity | *"**Honestly,** I don't think Redux fits here."* |

> ⚠️ **Overuse warning:** `literally` and `basically` are the 2 most overused words by non-native devs trying to sound American. Use each **once** per standup max. Otherwise you sound like a startup YouTuber.

